### Requests for the greetings API (IntelliJ HTTP client). The demo of Orgkeep must run: Keycloak on 8280, realm demo.

### 1. A token of Paul, for the catalogs prod and sandbox, as an application of the realm owner gets it.
# The login client of the demo realm is "demo" (the realm name); the password grant is on for the demo only.
# Full or lightweight, depending on the "Lightweight tokens" switch of the login client (dashboard, Login client page).
POST http://localhost:8280/realms/demo/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=demo&username=paul&password=password&scope=openid prod sandbox

> {% client.global.set("token", response.body.access_token); %}

### 2. The greetings API: how the token was verified, the size of the Authorization header, the rights and quotas read.
GET http://localhost:8290/greetings
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 3. The introspection the API makes in lightweight mode, by hand: the credentials of the catalog prod.
# The secret comes from the dashboard (page of the catalog prod, "Generate a secret").
POST http://localhost:8280/realms/demo/protocol/openid-connect/token/introspect
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded
Authorization: Basic prod {{catalogSecret}}

token={{token}}
